# Deployed Chat

Before finishing edits under these globs, read and satisfy:

[`apps/sim/app/(interfaces)/chat/REGRESSION_CHECKLIST.md`](apps/sim/app/(interfaces)/chat/REGRESSION_CHECKLIST.md)

## Non-negotiable contracts (do not regress)

### Thread row (`leftNavThread.tsx`)

- Never reintroduce a per-thread refresh (`RefreshCw`) button next to the ⋮ menu.
- Never hide Export behind `isActive &&`. Always render Export when `onExportChat` is provided; use `disabled={!isActive}` for inactive threads.
- Do not add Copy link back to the thread ⋮ menu.

### Landing copy (`clip-description.ts` / `DeployedChatLanding.tsx`)

- Landing shows welcome message only — not chat `description`.
- `resolveDeployedChatLandingDescription` must not take or prefer `description`.

### Start-block summary (`ArenaDeployedChat.tsx`)

- “Inputs received: …” is `type: 'user'` with `isStartBlockInputsSummary: true` so assistant actions (copy / regenerate / feedback) do not apply.

### Feedback markdown links (`markdown-renderer.tsx`)

- Plain links only — no URL hover popover. Hover color uses `--color-ds-text-link-hover`.

## Edit discipline

- Prefer surgical diffs. Do not rewrite entire ThreadRow / welcome / feedback blocks for a one-line change.
- One feature per commit when possible. Do not bundle unrelated chrome changes into a catch-all commit.
- After merges into this area, re-check the thread-history and landing sections of the checklist even if there were no conflict markers.
